    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Hi Naomi,</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">The message is <a href=\"https://github.com/THLfi/read.gt3x/blob/master/R/utils.R#L213\" title=\"generated\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/THLfi/read.gt3x/blob/master/R/utils.R%23L213&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792488704840000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0hPYZfNB8lzxYKcJFKW8jc\">generated</a> by R package read.gt3x, which GGIR uses as a dependency. So, the problem is likely specific to the file (or read.gt3x although not likely) and not to GGIR.</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Note that it is not an error but a message() and a warning(), which is not the same. Messages  and warnings are send without stopping the code, errors are send in conjunction with stopping the code.</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">So, it might be that read.gt3x and GGIR were still able to generate useful output? </div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Did you investigate the files with ActiLife or any other tool ActiGraph provides? I think that is the best starting point for an investigation.</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Best,</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Vincent</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(107,107,107)\">Dr. Vincent van Hees | Independent consultant | <