  {
   "id": "EbDImKqvAAAJ",
   "from": "Naomi Chapman",
   "author": "e2b64d7fa46d584e",
   "date": "2025-03-11T07:26:40Z",
   "subject": "Hi Re: [GGIR] Problem with reading .gt3x file in GGIR function dotorcomma",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi Vincent <div><br></div><div>Thank you for your response. Unfortunately the code didn&#39;t continue to run after this message/warning appeared. Yes I have been able to open the files in Actilife and analyse them using their software however for consistency need to run these files through GGIR as I did with the other set. <br><br></div><div>This is the code I have used to run the other files with no issues. </div><div><br></div><div>library(GGIR)<br>GGIR(mode=c(1,2,3,4,5),<br>  datadir=&quot;C:/Users/nchapman/Documents/GGIR data&quot;,<br>  outputdir=&quot;C:/Users/nchapman/Documents/GGIR test output working&quot;,<br>  do.report=c(2,5), <br>  <br>  #part1<br>  idloc=6,<br>  dynrange=NULL,<br>  do.enmo = TRUE,<br>  acc.metric = &quot;ENMO&quot;,<br>  <br>  #part2  <br>  strategy=2,<br>  includedaycrit=8,<br>  qwindow=c(0,24),<br>  do.imp=TRUE,    <br>  mvpathreshold=c(69.1),<br>  excludefirstlast=FALSE,<br>  <br>  #Part 3 and 4<br>  timethreshold=(5),<br>  anglethreshold=5,<br>  ignorenonwear=TRUE,<br>  def.noc.sleep=1, <br>  <br>  #Part5<br>  threshold.lig=c(47.4),<br>  threshold.mod=c(69.1),<br>  threshold.vig=c(258.7) ,<br>  bout.criter=0.8,<br>  <a href=\"http://boutcriter.in\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://boutcriter.in&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792488704845000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3POwI_5XR4LOI5ziHcJMuD\">boutcriter.in</a>=0.9,<br>  boutcriter.lig=0.8,<br>  boutcriter.mvpa=0.8,<br>  <a href=\"http://boutdur.in\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://boutdur.in&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792488704845000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1j-seXQS0WehMy-yTxkfPb\">boutdur.in</a>=c(1, 10, 30),<br>  boutdur.lig=c(1, 10),<br>  boutdur.mvpa=c(1, 10),<br>  includedaycrit.part5=8,<br>  part5_agg2_60seconds = TRUE,<br>  <br>  #visual report<br>  timewindow=c(&quot;MM&quot;),<br>  visualreport=TRUE,<br>  week_weekend_aggregate.part5=TRUE)</div><div><br></div><div>Do you have any other suggestions? </div><div>Thanks</div><div>Naomi </div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Saturday, 8 March 2025 at 00:00:14 UTC+8 Vincent van Hees wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Hi Naomi,</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">The message is <a href=\"https://github.com/THLfi/read.gt3x/blob/master/R/utils.R#L213\" title=\"generated\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/THLfi/read.gt3x/blob/master/R/utils.R%23L213&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792488704845000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0KpgNO17UHM_JAPNsx4hEq\">generated</a> by R package read.gt3x, which GGIR uses as a dependency. So, the problem is likely specific to the file (or read.gt3x although not likely) and not to GGIR.</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Note that it is not an error but a message() and a warning(), which is not the same. Messages  and warnings are send without stopping the code, errors are send in conjunction with stopping the code.</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">So, it might be that read.gt3x and GGIR were still able to generate useful output? </div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Did you investigate the files with ActiLife or any other tool ActiGraph provides? I think that is the best starting point for an investigation.</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Best,</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-