     "<div><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-weight:400;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">Hi Naomi,</span><span style=\"display:inline!important\"><br></span></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-weight:400;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></span></div><blockquote style=\"border-left:3px solid rgb(200,200,200);border-top-color:rgb(200,200,200);border-right-color:rgb(200,200,200);border-bottom-color:rgb(200,200,200);padding-left:10px;color:rgb(102,102,102)\"><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;display:inline!important\">files in Actilife and analyse them using their software however for consistency need to run these files through GGIR as I did with the other set.</span><br></div></blockquote><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">I did not ask you to replace GGIR for ActiLife, but to use ActiLife to investigate the issue. If ActiLife is able to process the data then there is probably no issue with the file itself.</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">If read.gt3x is not able to process the file, as your warning message indicates, then it is read.gt3x and not GGIR that cannot handle the file.</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Does the issue apply to all your files or only a few? If it is only a few then I guess it is a file corruption problem. If it is all then maybe you used a ActiGraph version that read.gt3x was not designed for. In either case, consider using ActiLife to export to the raw data to .csv format and then process those csv files with GGIR. You can gunzip the files to reduce storage space if needed.</div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Best,</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Vincent</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">\r\n    <div>\r\n        <div><div><br></div></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(107,107,107)\">Dr. Vincent van Hees | Independent consultant | </span><a title=\"https://accelting.com/\" href=\"https://accelting.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://accelting.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792488704851000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2RChckrhOOjo5C4ORsMkzI\">https://accelting.com/</a><br></div><div><img alt=\"image\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/RpackageGGIR/attach/1e9c16f8d110c/image?part=0.1.1&amp;view=1\"><br></div>\r\n    </div>\r\n    \r\n            <div>\r\n        \r\n            </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div>\r\n        On Tuesday, 11 March 2025 at 1:53 AM, Naomi Chapman &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">naomi.d...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br>\r\n        </div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><blockquote type=\"cite\">\r\n            Hi Vincent <div><br></div><div>Thank you for your response. Unfortunately the code didn&#39;t continue to run after this message/warning appeared. Yes I have been able to open the files in Actilife and analyse them using their software however for consistency need to run these files through GGIR as I did with the other set. <br><br></div><div>This is the code I have used to run the other files with no issues. </div><div><br></div><div>library(GGIR)<br>GGIR(mode=c(1,2,3,4,5),<br>  datadir=&quot;C:/Users/nchapman/Documents/GGIR data&quot;,<br>  outputdir=&quot;C:/Users/nchapman/Documents/GGIR test output working&quot;,<br>  do.report=c(2,5), <br>  <br>  #part1<br>  idloc=6,<br>  dynrange=NULL,<br>  do.enmo = TRUE,<br>  acc.metric = &quot;ENMO&quot;,<br>  <br>  #part2  <br>  strategy=2,<br>  includedaycrit=8,<br>  qwindow=c(0,24),<br>  do.imp=TRUE,    <br>  mvpathreshold=c(69.1),<br>  excludefirstlast=FALSE,<br>  <br>  #Part 3 and 4<br>  timethreshold=(5),<br>  anglethreshold=5,<br>  ignorenonwear=TRUE,<br>  def.noc.sleep=1, <br>  <br>  #Part5<br>  threshold.lig=c(47.4),<br>  threshold.mod=c(69.1),<br>  threshold.vig=c(258.7) ,<br>  bout.criter=0.8,<br>  <a href=\"http://boutcriter.in\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://boutcriter.in&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792488704852000&amp;usg=AOvVaw38pMEEiOyP9kC0fYVFE8dv\">boutcriter.in</a>=0.9,<br>  boutcriter.lig=0.8,<br>  boutcriter.mvpa=0.8,<br>  <a href=\"http://boutdur.in\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://boutdur.in&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792488704852000&amp;usg=AOvVaw31oggabaqYkL0h-nqsf694\">boutdur.in</a>=c(1, 10, 30),<br>  boutdur.lig=c(1, 10),<br>  boutdur.mvpa=c(1, 10),<br>  includedaycrit.part5=8,<br>  part5_agg2_60seconds = TRUE,<br>  <br>  #visual report<br>  timewindow=c(&quot;MM&quot;),<br>  visualreport=TRUE,<br>  week_weekend_aggregate.part5=TRUE)</div><div><br></div><div>Do you have any other suggestions? </div><div>Thanks</div><div>Naomi </div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div class=\"gmail_attr\" dir=\"auto\">On Saturday, 8 March 2025 at 00:00:14 UTC+8 Vincent van Hees wrote:<br></div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\" class=\"gmail_quote\"><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Hi Naomi,</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">The message is <a rel=\"noreferrer nofollow noopener\" title=\"generated\" href=\"https://github.com/THLfi/read.gt3x/blob/master/R/utils.R#L213\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/THLfi/read.gt3x/blob/master/R/utils.R%23L213&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792488704852000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3kTSrmREkp7OjPK4eafSdN\">generated</a> by R package read.gt3x, which GGIR uses as a dependency. So, the problem is likely specific to the file (or read.gt3x although not likely) and not to GGIR.</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Note that it is not an error but a message() and a warning(), which is not the same. Messages  and warnings are send without stopping the code, errors are send in conjunction with stopping the code.</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">So, it might be that read.gt3x and GGIR were still able to generate useful output? </div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Did you investigate the files with ActiLife or any other tool ActiGraph provides? I think that is the best starting point for an investigation.</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Best,</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Vincent</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(107,107,107)\">Dr. Vincent van Hees | Independent consultant | </span><a rel=\"noreferrer nofollow noopener\" href=\"https://accelting.com/\" title=\"https://accelting.com/\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://accelting.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792488704852000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1jVzTivuxGb0k1N9BKSBOs\">https://accelting.com/</a><br></div><div><img alt=\"image\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/RpackageGGIR/attach/1a0355d596fa6/image?part=0.1.1&amp;view=1\"><br></div>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n            <div>\r\n\r\n            </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div></div><div>\r\n        On Friday, 7 March 2025 at 7:34 AM, Naomi Chapman &lt;<a rel=\"noreferrer nofollow noopener\">naomi.d...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br>\r\n        </div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\">\r\n            <span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><font color=\"#000000\">Hi</font></span></span><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><br></span></span></span></div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><font color=\"#000000\">I am currently trying to analyse some GT3x raw Actigraph data that was downloaded from devices in 2020 and keep running into an error message which I don&#39;t know how to fix. Does anyone know what I need to do to fix this error and analyse the file? </font></span></span></div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></span></span></div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><font color=\"#000000\">The error message is: </font></span></span></div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><br></span></span></span></div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"> Negative samples estimated, dates are wrong in info, using maximum samples (100 days)\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Error in g.dotorcomma(datafile, dformat, mon, rmc.dec = params_rawdata[[&quot;rmc.dec&quot;]]) :\r\n  Problem with reading .gt3x file in GGIR function dotorcomma</span></span></span></div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><br></span></span></span></div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><font color=\"#000000\">Thanks</font></span></span></div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><font color=\"#000000\">Naomi </font></span></span></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\">\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;R package GGIR&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a rel=\"noreferrer nofollow noopener\">RpackageGGIR...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion, visit <a rel=\"noreferrer nofollow noopener\" href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/RpackageGGIR/23305cc6-0a6f-45db-8ff9-5e081932f674n%40googlegroups.com\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/RpackageGGIR/23305cc6-0a6f-45db-8ff9-5e081932f674n%2540googlegroups.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792488704852000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2J7neEZBkhMfVWj5QeRL78\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/RpackageGGIR/23305cc6-0a6f-45db-8ff9-5e081932f674n%40googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\n\r\n        </blockquote><br>\r\n    </div></blockquote></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\